--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
=== PARITY === (all 3 web hooks ported — web/src/api/hooks/useFeedback.ts)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Reads / queries (1):
  [x] useFeedbackList   -> FeedbackStore.feedbackList(params)
                           GET /admin/feedback ?status=&category=&limit=&offset=
                           query builder = feedbackQuery (web buildQuery: status/category
                           sent only when non-blank; limit/offset sent whenever present,
                           incl. explicit 0). cache key = feedbackCacheKey (web
                           feedbackKeys.list tuple, null-coalesced). TTL = 1m =
                           DEFAULT_QUERY_CLIENT_CONFIG staleTime 60_000.

Mutations / actions (2):
  [x] useSubmitFeedback -> FeedbackStore.submitFeedback(input)
                           POST /feedback ; body = FeedbackSubmitInput (nulls dropped,
                           empty strings kept = JSON.stringify semantics).
                           NO cache invalidation — web hook declares none (submit modal
                           and admin queue are independent surfaces). Verified by
                           submitFeedbackPostsBodyAndLeavesCacheUntouched + store test
                           submitDelegatesAndDoesNotRefreshAnyFeed.
  [x] useUpdateFeedback -> FeedbackStore.updateFeedback(input)
                           PATCH /admin/feedback/{id} ; body = FeedbackUpdateInput
                           (only provided fields; forward_to_github only when set).
                           onSuccess invalidates the WHOLE Feedback partition (clear) =
                           web invalidateQueries(feedbackKeys.all). Store refreshes every
                           observed feed. Verified by
                           updateFeedbackPatchesByIdAndInvalidatesWholePartition +
                           updateDelegatesAndRefreshesEveryObservedFeed.

NOTE: the prompt body lists useSubmitFeedback under "Reads / queries"; the web
hook uses `useMutation` (a write), so it is ported as a mutation. All 3 hooks are
covered either way — counts above reflect the true read/mutation split.

SI: no feedback field is unit-bearing (ids, RFC3339 timestamps, free text, status enum,
    opaque recent_errors JSON blob) — payloads round-trip verbatim, no SI conversion.

Out of scope (no web hook exists): GET /admin/feedback/{id} single-row read.

